---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
const updated = 'September 11, 2026';
---
<Base path="/privacy" title="Privacy"
      description="What Austin Devs collects on this site and in its apps, and what it does not.">
  <section class="panel" data-route="/privacy" data-current>
    <div class="inner prose">
      <h1 class="page-title">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This covers austindevs.com and the applications built and owned by {SITE.legal}. The short version:
        very little is collected, none of it is sold, and none of it is used to build a profile of you.
      </p>
      <p class="note">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        Analytics are handled by Google Analytics with its default configuration. That means Google collects
        the usual measurement data, including a device identifier, approximate location derived from IP
        address, pages viewed, and referrer. No custom identifiers, no marketing pixels, and no cross-site
        advertising integrations are added on top of it.
      </p>
      <p>
        A single functional cookie named <code>ad_theme</code> stores which of the site's color themes you
        were shown, so the site looks the same when you come back. It holds one short word, nothing about
        you, and clearing it simply picks a new theme.
      </p>

      <h2>The contact form</h2>
      <p>
        The form collects your name, email address, and your message, and sends them by email so they can be
        read and replied to. They are not added to a marketing list and no newsletter follows.
      </p>
      <p>
        The form is protected by Cloudflare Turnstile, which runs in invisible mode and checks that the
        submission comes from a person rather than a script. Cloudflare processes data for this purpose as
        described in the <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/en-gb/turnstile-privacy-policy/">Cloudflare
        Turnstile Privacy Addendum</a>. Turnstile does not use this data for advertising or cross-site
        tracking.
      </p>

      <h2>Applications</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.legal} builds and operates a number of applications, and this policy applies to those owned by
        {SITE.legal}. The set changes over time, so it is not enumerated here; each application identifies
        its operator in its own interface.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where an application has accounts, it holds the details needed to run it, typically a name and an
        email address, along with whatever content you choose to put into it. That content belongs to you.
        It is not sold, rented, or shared for anyone else's marketing, and it is not used to train models
        for third parties.
      </p>
      <p>
        Applications built for a client under contract are operated by that client, and their own privacy
        policy applies rather than this one.
      </p>

      <h2>Service providers</h2>
      <p>
        Running any of this involves a small number of vendors acting on instructions: hosting and network
        providers, email delivery, and the analytics and bot protection described above. They receive only
        what they need to perform their function.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention</h2>
      <p>
        Contact form messages are kept as ordinary email correspondence for as long as they are useful.
        Application data is kept while the account exists. Analytics retention follows Google Analytics'
        own default settings.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask what is held about you, ask for it to be corrected, or ask for it to be deleted, and
        that request will be honored where there is no legal reason to keep it. Analytics can be blocked with
        the Google Analytics opt-out add-on or any content blocker, and the site works normally without it.
        The theme cookie can be cleared at any time in your browser.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>None of this is directed at children under 13, and information is not knowingly collected from them.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If this policy changes materially, the date above changes with it.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
